API Testing Automation Project (Lesson 31)

Project Structure

Endpoint.py – Contains all API endpoint URLs.
data.py– Contains request bodies, payload templates, and standard headers.
test_todo_api.py– Main test script executing the full end-to-end API testing workflow.
README – Project documentation and usage guide.

End-to-End Test Workflow

The main test script (test_todo_api.py) runs the following 4 sequential steps in a single execution flow:

1. Register Non-Admin User**
   Sends a 'POST' request to the registration API using user data defined in `data.py`.
   Verifies that the user registration status code is success (`201 Created` / `200 OK`).

2. Login with Registered User**
   Sends a `POST` request to the login endpoint using the newly registered credentials.
   Extracts and stores the "Bearer JWT Token" from the server response for upcoming authenticated requests.

3. Add Account Balance
    Sends an authenticated `POST` request to the balance endpoint.
   Passes the retrieved Bearer Token in `headers` alongside the payment payload (`amount`, `card details`).

4. Check & Assert Account Balance
   Verifies that the balance API responds with status code `200 OK`.
   Asserts and prints the updated balance response to ensure account details are accurate.


